{"name":"Golden Banner","hex":"#fcc62a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"banner","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flag or standard used by a military commander, monarch or nation.","The military unit under such a flag or standard."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Exceptional; very good."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banner"}],"entries":[{"title":"Banner","blocks":[{"text":"A banner is a flag or another piece of cloth bearing a symbol, logo, slogan or another message. A flag whose design is the same as the shield in a coat of arms is a banner of arms. A bar-shaped piece of advertising material sporting a name, slogan, or other marketing message is also a banner. Banners may hang from horizontal or vertical flagpoles, be stretched between two poles, be attached to windows or buildings, or be towed behind aircraft."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Banners_of_Knights_of_the_Thistle.jpg/330px-Banners_of_Knights_of_the_Thistle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banner","wikidata":"Q806880"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.